<title>UK: Refuge H1 premium income higher.</title>
<headline>Refuge H1 premium income higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.4		    vs n/a</p>
<p>Total periodic</p>
<p> premium income	   92.36		  vs 91.84</p>
<p>Total single</p>
<p> premium income	   15.80		  vs 10.73</p>
<p> Total ordinary business 47.13		     vs 45.68</p>
<p> Industrial business     45.23		     vs 46.16</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 18</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 8</p>
<p>Note - Refuge Group Plc said there were &quot;some encouraging signs of a return of consumer confidence to the pensions market&quot;.</p>
